    "https://www.washcoll.edu/people_departments/offices/human-resources/employment/index.php?jobId=bde235c3-0efe-bbdf-f91e-369b85de44b8": {
      "title": "Employment",
      "description": "Employment at Washington College | Washington College Click to Open Menu Click to Toggle Search Search Input Single Button Submit Search Academics Academics Overview Schools & Departments Majors & Minors Writing at Washington Library & Archives Senior Capstone Experience Study Abroad Summer Term Admissions & Aid Apply Visit & Virtual Tour Upcoming Events Admitted Students International Students Transfer Students Scholarships Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Request Information Admissions Team Campus Life First Year Experience Arts & Culture Find Your Fit Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Community & Belonging Civic Engagement Student Support Sustainability Experiential Learning Research at Washington Center for Career Development Rose O'Neill Literary House Starr Center for the Study of the American Experience Center for Environment and Society Geospatial Innovation Program River and Field Campus Athletics Varsity Athletics Game Schedule Washington College Sports MyWashColl Directories News Events About Give Academy of Lifelong Learning Current Students Faculty & Staff Admitted Students Prospective Parents & Family Parents & Family Alumni Donors Chestertown Community People & Departments Offices Human Resources Employment Employment Welcome to the official site for employment opportunities at Washington College! \n                           Here at Washington College, we are a community of administrators, faculty, and staff\n                           that are engaged and committed to the success of our students!  We offer an excellent\n                           work environment with a stable Monday to Friday work week and offer generous leave\n                           programs to assist with work-life balance.  We encourage you to review this page often\n                           and apply for all positions that you have interest in. For assistance or additional questions, please reach out directly to Washington College's\n                           Office of Human Resources at hrFREEwashcoll . To narrow the number of positions displayed, use the filter to sort the position types\n                           by Faculty, Contingent Faculty, Regular Full Time, and more. Current Positions EEO and Title IX Statement Washington College values our students, faculty, and staff, and strives to recruit,\n                           develop, and retain the most talented people. Washington College does not discriminate\n                           in employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation,\n                           transgender status, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, veteran status,\n                           or any other legally protected status in accordance with applicable federal, state\n                           and/or local laws. For information on Washington College's Title IX compliance, please\n                           visit https://www.washcoll.edu/title-ix/ . Other Information Employment is contingent upon completion of a successful background check and establishment\n                           of identity and verification of employment eligibility as required by the Immigration\n                           Reform and Control Act of 1986. It is the policy of Washington College to provide\n                           reasonable accommodations. If you require any accommodations to participate in any\n                           part of the hiring process, please contact hrFREEwashcoll . Human Resources Team 410-778-7260 [email protected] 300 Washington Avenue *Federal legislation requires institutions of higher education to inform prospective\n                           members of our campus community about its most recent crime statistics, campus safety\n                           tips, and other important information. Click Annual Security and Fire Safety Report here for information about safety and security at Washington College. 300 Washington Avenue Chestertown, Maryland 21620 Maps and Directions 410-778-2800 Contact Us Youtube Facebook Twitter Instagram Employment Newsroom Virtual Tour Accessibility Consumer Information Privacy Title IX © 2026 Washington College ©"
    },
