      "title": "Employment at Washington College",
      "description": "Employment at Washington College | Washington College Click to Open Menu Click to Toggle Search Search Input Single Button Submit Search Academics Open the Academics menu Academics Overview Schools & Departments Majors & Minors Writing at Washington Library & Archives Senior Capstone Experience Study Abroad Summer Term Admissions & Aid Open the Admissions & Aid menu Apply Visit & Virtual Tour Upcoming Events Admitted Students International Students Transfer Students Scholarships Financial Aid Tuition and Fees Request Information Admissions Team Campus Life Open the Campus Life menu First Year Experience Arts & Culture Find Your Fit Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Community & Belonging Civic Engagement Student Support Sustainability Experiential Learning Open the Experiential Learning menu Research at Washington Center for Career Development Rose O'Neill Literary House Starr Center for the Study of the American Experience Center for Environment and Society Geospatial Innovation Program River and Field Campus Athletics Open the Athletics menu Varsity Athletics Game Schedule Washington College Sports MyWashColl Directories News Events About Give Information For Click to Open Academy of Lifelong Learning Current Students Faculty & Staff Admitted Students Prospective Parents & Family Parents & Family Alumni Donors Chestertown Community People & Departments Offices Human Resources Employment Employment Welcome to the official site for employment opportunities at Washington College! \n                           Here at Washington College, we are a community of administrators, faculty, and staff\n                           that are engaged and committed to the success of our students!  We offer an excellent\n                           work environment with a stable Monday to Friday work week and offer generous leave\n                           programs to assist with work-life balance.  We encourage you to review this page often\n                           and apply for all positions that you have interest in. For assistance or additional questions, please reach out directly to Washington College's\n                           Office of Human Resources at hr@washcoll.edu . To narrow the number of positions displayed, use the filter to sort the position types\n                           by Faculty, Contingent Faculty, Regular Full Time, and more. Current Positions Back to Job Openings Visiting Assistant Professor of Marketing Apply Share Link copied The Washington College Department of Business Management seeks candidates for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor position in Marketing beginning August 2027 and annually renewable. The successful candidate will join our faculty following the historic Fall 2026 launch of the new Warehime School of Business, providing the incoming faculty member a unique opportunity to help shape the trajectory and growth of our programs. The position carries a teaching load of three courses per semester, including a combination of Principles of Marketing, Marketing Research Methods, and Managerial Statistics. Additionally, the candidate will develop and teach upper-level marketing electives. Candidates with the expertise to teach upper-level courses focusing on Artificial Intelligence (AI) in marketing or Food Marketing are highly preferred. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the college-wide first year writing and research program. Candidates should have a Ph.D or D.B.A. in Marketing, a related field such as Management or Sales might be considered (A.B.D.’s welcomed). The successful candidate should be enthusiastic about teaching in a liberal-arts environment (with an emphasis on critical thinking, writing, speaking, and faculty-student interaction). This is an opportunity for candidates who would thrive in a collegial environment that supports research, encourages interdisciplinary efforts within and beyond the department, and provides mentorship for junior faculty. Our department values the contributions of a diverse and global faculty and believes that multiple perspectives offer our students the best tools for critical thinking. Washington College is a top-tier, private, selective, independent liberal-arts college located in historic Chestertown on Maryland’s Eastern Shore, within easy driving distance to Washington, D.C., Baltimore, and Philadelphia. Founded in 1782 under the patronage of George Washington, this tenth-oldest college in the country celebrates a rich heritage of producing citizen-leaders who have made significant impacts in their chosen endeavors. Its location central to the Chesapeake Bay provides both academic and recreational opportunities. Business Management is viewed as a liberal art at Washington College; we characterize it as the active liberal art, emphasizing social responsibility and the global nature of business. Our mission is to activate the liberal arts to inspire business innovation, global leadership, and social impact. Essential Functions: Teach three marketing courses per semester including a combination of Principles of Marketing, Marketing Research Methods, and Managerial Statistics The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the college-wide first year writing and research program. Qualifications: Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Marketing or a related field such as Sales. 2+ years teaching college-age students in a college or university setting preferred. Enthusiasm about teaching in a liberal-arts environment (with an emphasis on critical thinking, writing, speaking, and faculty-student interaction). Salary: $63,000 - $77,250 Apply EEO and Title IX Statement Washington College values our students, faculty, and staff, and strives to recruit,\n                           develop, and retain the most talented people. Washington College does not discriminate\n                           in employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation,\n                           transgender status, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, veteran status,\n                           or any other legally protected status in accordance with applicable federal, state\n                           and/or local laws. For information on Washington College's Title IX compliance, please\n                           visit https://www.washcoll.edu/title-ix/ . Other Information Employment is contingent upon completion of a successful background check and establishment\n                           of identity and verification of employment eligibility as required by the Immigration\n                           Reform and Control Act of 1986. It is the policy of Washington College to provide\n                           reasonable accommodations. If you require any accommodations to participate in any\n                           part of the hiring process, please contact hr@washcoll.edu . Human Resources Team 410-778-7260 hr@washcoll.edu 300 Washington Avenue *Federal legislation requires institutions of higher education to inform prospective\n                           members of our campus community about its most recent crime statistics, campus safety\n                           tips, and other important information. Click Annual Security and Fire Safety Report here for information about safety and security at Washington College. By using this website you consent to Washington College’s privacy policy. Review Privacy Policy Dismiss 300 Washington Avenue Chestertown, Maryland 21620 Maps and Directions 410-778-2800 Contact Us Youtube Facebook Twitter Instagram Employment Newsroom Virtual Tour Accessibility Consumer Information Privacy Title IX © 2026 Washington College"
    }
  },
